 cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Preserve shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Retain metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin underlines over every in-document character and expanded-tab cell, retaining text, colors and widths. Reserve vertical bars for line-end and empty-line padding.\n- Retain selected narrow UI repairs, completion suffixes, supersampling and bounded diagnostic comparisons.\n- Public APIs, method signatures, dependency declarations, diagnostic interfaces and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged.\n\n## Focused coverage and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Verify restored files match pinned-dev hashes and that documentation/changelog retain both dev and feature content.\n- Run restored capture-exporter regressions first on GitHub, retaining unsafe-path, changed-file, capacity, partial-evidence and failed-capture controls. Reuse existing tests; add tests only for a demonstrated uncovered failure.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret, completion-spacing, menu-viewport, checkbox/selector and capture-diagnostics regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head quality, type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and existing floors: **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem and debt baselines.\n- Obtain a trusted isolated GitHub capture of the reconciled candidate at 208×47 cells and 1280×800 pixels. Require every geometry assertion and individual full-PNG verdict for all **46 scenes**; retain picker comparisons.\n- Bind all evidence to the actual candidate, checkpoint, task, plan, dependencies and current dev base. Earlier capture-stage pending fields do not invalidate the predecessor’s final receipt, but that receipt cannot certify new content.\n\n## Independent review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh current-base plan review before coding, followed by complete independent implementation review.\n- Assess every diff continuation, explicitly including `tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py`, `svg_evidence.py`, `visual_lifecycle.py`, associated helpers and capture integration. Track assessed ranges separately from retrieved pages.\n- Complete companion source/test assessment and verify exact-commit CI, installed-source identity, activation, rollback and waiting-agent recovery evidence. Preserve genuine-input and security holds.\n- Preserve review progress and evidence across retries. Incomplete assessment must remain a review-routing issue; it supplies no product defect or correction approval.\n- Preserve provenance, dependency barriers, credentials, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals. The reconciliation choice grants none of these approvals.\n- After complete independent approval and required gates, use the trusted merge workflow. Continue coordinator monitoring of PR #9, recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR until all merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ab2679dc24629062eb4499ec69be0ecedf4768a71b27496b508cfb6baf84cd40","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and validate the saved diagnostic checkpoint\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`, preserving the complete feature and authenticated history.\n\nPublished head `98508973146e4137a88eaacff9a4cc13f8e84d9c` has passing non-review checks but a rejected visual review. The inspected PNG shows separate ruler and gutter labels; secondary-caret visibility remains unresolved. Its geometry lacks the diagnostics now present in the saved checkpoint.\n\nThe recorded **Preserve ruler** and **Diagnose first** choices settle the approach. No material question remains unanswered.\n\n## Implementation\n\n- Remove only the extra blank line at EOF in `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, retaining one terminating newline and every test, fixture and assertion.\n- Preserve the saved caret diagnostics in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`: actual selections, primary identity, preferred columns, focus, keyboard mode, scrolling, viewport and terminal-cell mapping; exact widget/compositor text, colors and style flags. Keep expected fixture state separate from observations.\n- Preserve single-export integration in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_capture.py`: retain exact raw, framed and supersampling SVG inputs, ordinary PNG hashes, renderer settings and processing metadata through atomic geometry JSON publication.\n- Retain existing bounds: nine regions/carets, 24 rows, 208 cells, 256 parsed SVG elements, 512 KiB reduced diagnostics and 4 MiB combined lossless SVG inputs. Missing probes, clipping, limits and failures must explicitly identify incomplete evidence.\n- Preserve the mounted tab/database-switch ruler regression and scene metadata distinguishing the active-column label from the first gutter/text row. Retain overlap, shifted-mapping and missing-label negative controls.\n- Preserve current-dev capture safeguards, recovered source/documentation, selected narrow UI repairs, supersampling and picker comparisons. Retain the managed changelog fragment without changing package versions.\n- Keep collection observational: no new refocusing, event draining, retries, timing changes, scene-state correction or production/export presentation changes.\n\nPublic APIs, signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic JSON additions remain additive.\n\n## Feature requirements retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without spawning cursors; independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Multiple cursors per row, selection merging, independent movement/editing, atomic undo/redo, bounded history and reset cleanup. Shift+Up/Down toggles only the exact projected position.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary carets preserving SQL, whitespace, expanded tabs, colors, widths and mapping: underlines in every in-document cell; bars only in line-end or empty-line padding.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Obtain fresh independent plan review before source correction.\n- On GitHub, first check formatting and run the existing multicursor-diagnostics, ruler, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions. Verify collection preserves state and distinguishes missing evidence from observed absent caret marks.\n- Retain Unicode, combining-character, wide-cell, expanded-tab, clipping, unavailable-compositor, limit, single-export, atomic-publication and readiness/geometry rejection coverage.\n- Run focused multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret and completion regressions, followed by required quality, type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks.\n- Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branches**, **98.92% combined** and **99.22% statements**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines.\n- Use the trusted temporary-candidate GitHub capture route. Bind evidence to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies and run; verify extracted SVG and PNG hashes.\n- Independently inspect the new caret layers and full PNG to identify the first failing layer. Recorded underline styles alone cannot establish visibility. Inconclusive observations remain unresolved; a demonstrated production/export repair requires renewed independent planning.\n- Submit the ruler evidence for independent reassessment while retaining the current rejection. Require all **46** geometry checks and individual full-PNG verdicts before correction publication.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Complete independent assessment of every feature diff continuation, diagnostic/capture module, associated test and companion implementation. Track assessed ranges separately from retrieved pages.\n- Revalidate changed heads and dev bases. Preserve complete provenance, dependency barriers, credentials, genuine-input holds, owner vetoes and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy companion completion, recorded independent resolutions, safe activation and recovery of agents waiting solely on routine choices. Preserve frozen rollout sources and completed deployments.\n- Monitor PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work and every task-related repair PR through successful merges into `dev` and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that overall objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"ba2ca6de6e000df75238880cfd1237b0f8fb42b4d83747a5e9cacaf901396d87","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and validate the correction checkpoint\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue against pinned dev `7142aac73dbc26fb0195b61e1dce7bcf8aa19e5a`, preserving the complete feature, useful saved edits, recovered source/documentation, and authenticated task history.\n\nComplete assigned feedback binds failed CI and visual rejection to published head `43852778725dc1bb13b91b7a735cafaf9bacf5f6`. It does not validate unpublished checkpoint changes.\n\nThe recorded **Narrow gate repairs** and **Faithful diagnostics** choices settle this correction sequence. No material owner question remains. First validate the saved journal correction and faithful diagnostics; use fresh GitHub evidence before selecting remaining presentation, export, focus, or layout repairs.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- Preserve the saved correction in `analytics_toolkit/sql_explorer/journal_screen.py`: empty failed reads show the warning alone; successful empty reads show “No matching journal entries.” Populated pages retain their count and any warning. Preserve stale-generation rejection, recovery, controls, and query behavior.\n- Preserve `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`’s cell-based cropping: retain combining suffixes with a completely retained base, including across differently styled spans; preserve original colors/styles and expanded-tab cells; represent partially clipped wide cells faithfully without mutating observations.\n- Retain saved fixes for test-variable shadowing, compound assertions, long lines, formatting, and scene-collector complexity. Preserve every assertion, negative control, fixture value, diagnostic ordering, and failure-containment behavior. Do not add suppressions or change debt baselines.\n- Preserve the added command-caret and new-file diagnostics, associated scene/capture integration, and ruler lifecycle snapshots. Record actual focus, selections, preferred columns, scroll, cell mapping, widget/compositor rows and styles, screen ancestry, resolved alignment, geometry, pending layout flags, queue sizes, row lengths, and dependency versions.\n- Keep observations bounded: nine regions/carets, 24 rows, 208 cells, 256 parsed SVG elements, 512 KiB reduced diagnostics, 8 KiB lifecycle snapshots, and existing lossless SVG/comparison budgets. Explicitly identify unavailable, clipped, omitted, or incomplete evidence.\n- Preserve single-export ownership, exact raw/framed/supersampling SVG inputs, PNG hashes, renderer settings, and atomic geometry publication through the existing artifact route. Do not refocus, drain queues, retry assertions, alter timing, or force scene state.\n- Retain the managed changelog fragment and current-dev capture/provenance safeguards. Fully read affected files through their final continuation before any subsequent edit.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies, diagnostic compatibility, and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual support remain unchanged. Diagnostic additions are additive.\n\n## Complete feature requirements retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without spawning cursors; independent preferred columns, short-line clamping, reversal, and boundaries.\n- Independent multicursor movement/editing, multiple cursors per row, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggling, atomic undo/redo, bounded history metadata, and reset cleanup.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary underlines over all in-document characters, spaces, and expanded-tab cells; bars only in line-end/empty-line padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selection/scroll/ruler mapping, and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve the selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, ruler presentation/reassessment, picker correction, supersampling, comparison evidence, and recovered tests/documentation. Partial implementation supplies no additional scope.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nPrivate workers execute no programs, tests, installs, or rendering.\n\n1. Obtain fresh independent whole-plan review before coding.\n2. On GitHub, first run diagnostic lint/format checks and the existing multicursor-diagnostics, scene-observations, ruler/visual-state, and journal-status regressions.\n3. Require Unicode, cross-span combining marks, wide-cell clipping, expanded tabs, style preservation, missing compositor, bounds, unavailable probes, non-mutation, journal failure/recovery, and stale-result controls to pass.\n4. Retain the strict ruler focus and widget/compositor equality assertions. Capture their original failing-state snapshots without recollection. Obtain exact-candidate GitHub observations before changing focus, widths, assertions, or lifecycle behavior.\n5. Capture command-caret, keyboard-multicursor, and new-file scenes with the saved diagnostics. Independently compare widget, compositor, SVG, and full PNG layers. Recorded underline flags alone do not establish visible carets. New-file alignment must be traced through actual resolved screen/dialog layout before selecting its repair.\n6. Run adjacent selection/clipboard, history/reset, native-renderer caret, completion, menu, checkbox/selector, SVG-evidence, supersampling, capture-lifecycle, and restored safeguard regressions.\n7. Require exact-head quality/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK, and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON, **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem floors, and debt baselines. Failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n\nBind all observations to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, GitHub run, and artifact hashes. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved. Any demonstrated remaining repair requires a concrete renewed plan and independent review.\n\n## Review, publication, and completion\n\n- Keep existing visual rejections in force. After reviewed repairs, obtain fresh independent complete-feature/source review and all **46** candidate-bound geometry checks and individual full **1280×800 PNG** verdicts at the **208×47** terminal grid. Historical captures cannot certify new edits.\n- Assess every diff continuation and companion implementation; track assessed coverage separately from retrieved pages. Revalidate changed heads and dev bases.\n- Preserve complete provenance, credentials, genuine-input/security holds, owner veto/cancel, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable real-owner exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility, activation and rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses, the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator, idle exit, and coordinator-owned drain pause.\n- Use trusted publication and merge mechanisms only after required gates. Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, the recommendation-policy/restart companion work, and every qualifying repair PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a7052639e6cfc2694f714789db06ed529351f2900652de1bbba7dac4277eacb6","text":"# Preserve SQL Explorer and trace the remaining ruler failures\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from published head `c1976299ef64679a9e1335825800277a3c6e9f15` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nApply the selected **Trace lifecycle** sequence: correct confirmed lint/format findings, restore inherited dev safeguards, and collect bounded GitHub evidence before choosing a focus or row-width repair. No material implementation question remains for this diagnostic checkpoint.\n\nCurrent logs establish unexpected editor focus and, on Textual 0.89.1, 205 widget cells versus 206 compositor cells. They do not establish callback execution order or the first padding divergence.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- In `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`, refactor `_targets` to assign the selected target list and return once. Preserve lazy scene-specific queries, target order, requested row counts, filtering, exceptions and diagnostic output. Resolve `PLR0911` without suppressions.\n- Apply canonical repository Ruff formatting to `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`. Preserve every fixture, assertion, parameter and Unicode/style negative control.\n- Add test-support instrumentation around the existing ruler regression and visual scene. Record callback scheduling and execution order for tab activation, database switching and deferred focus restoration; include active tab, focused-widget identity and remembered-focus identity before and after each observed callback.\n- Invoke each wrapped callback exactly once with its original arguments, return value and exception behavior. Preserve its scheduler and execution position. Install instrumentation before scene configuration and restore wrappers during cleanup; change no production tab/workspace behavior.\n- Extend ruler observations with original strip cell/character lengths, requested crop width, resulting lengths, region/content widths, scrollbar/gutter state and exact trailing text/style spans. Observe the strips already collected for that snapshot; do not pad, trim, rerender or normalize them.\n- Bound the lifecycle trace to 64 events and 8 KiB. Report overflow, unavailable probes and collection failures explicitly. Preserve the first failing snapshot alongside its trace; diagnostics must not replace the original assertion failure.\n- Retain exact focus and widget/compositor equality assertions, geometry checks and negative controls. Add no refocusing, sleeps, queue draining, retries or scene-state changes.\n- Restore `.github/agent/review_control.py` and the deleted `tests/repository/coordinator_scope.py` byte-for-byte from pinned dev. Retain dev’s coordinator-scope documentation plus the feature-specific activation section. Restore the three removed dev changelog entries while preserving all distinct feature entries and historical releases.\n- Fully read edited files through their final continuation before writing. Preserve recovered source/documentation and the useful checkpoint; record this correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package versions.\n\nPublic APIs, method signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive; existing fields and budgets retain their meaning.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without creating cursors, preserving independent preferred columns through short lines, reversal and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and document-reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve thin primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs; bars appear only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Retain selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, journal failure reporting, faithful combining-mark/style cropping, supersampling and lossless capture evidence. Remaining command-caret, ruler and new-file findings stay unresolved until fresh evidence supports a reviewed correction.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub evidence\n\nAll execution occurs on GitHub. Private workers execute no programs, tests, installs or rendering.\n\n- Test trace ordering, bounded retention, unavailable probes, cleanup and faithful forwarding of callback results/exceptions. Verify instrumentation preserves focus, text, selections, preferences, scroll and callback execution counts.\n- Test strip observations with unequal widths, trailing spaces, styled padding, combining marks and wide cells. Require recorded original bytes/styles and lengths to survive unchanged.\n- Run the instrumented ruler regression first on canonical Python 3.11/Textual 0.73.0 and Python 3.14/Textual 0.89.1, then the supported matrix. Retain expected failures and their original snapshots; diagnostic success does not require making the regression pass.\n- Run restored coordinator-scope regressions, adjacent ruler/scene observations, multicursor diagnostics, journal-status and capture-lifecycle tests. Follow with focused selection/clipboard, history/reset, native caret, completion, menu, checkbox/selector and SVG/supersampling regressions.\n- Require exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines. Failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n- Use the existing trusted temporary-candidate route and artifact transport. Bind observations to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependency versions, run and hashes. Preserve single-export ownership and atomic evidence publication.\n\nAfter independently assessing the new lifecycle, strip, command-caret and dialog evidence, produce a separate concrete repair plan for each demonstrated remaining cause. Inconclusive evidence remains unresolved.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding, followed by independent implementation review. Revalidate changed heads or dev bases.\n- Keep visual rejections in force. Before correction publication, require complete feature/source review and all **46** geometry checks and individual full **1280×800 PNG** verdicts at **208×47** cells. Historical captures cannot certify new edits.\n- Preserve complete authenticated history, question/options/answer records, provenance, credentials, owner veto/cancel, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator retains companion recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility and activation/rollback verification. Preserve notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit. Honor actual current runtime holds; historical pause statements neither establish nor release one. Preserve frozen rollout sources and completed deployments.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This diagnostic checkpoint does not complete that broader objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"243f9516de3a3cfd3dd817a81b491c72c30fcfcfc68c2c426fdcdee3e8488b3e","text":"# Correct the SQL Explorer harness and preserve the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `f04d007c090bff62a19a6c2adb7f91bc242d3ecc` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nImplement the recorded **Correct harness layers** choice. Current GitHub evidence identifies deferred focus restoration overriding scene initialization, and a comparison between raw widget output and styled compositor output. Correct those harness boundaries and the confirmed lint findings. Preserve production tab restoration and ruler presentation.\n\nNo material implementation question remains. The selected strategy supplies no plan, source, visual, protected-policy, or merge approval.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- **Order scene initialization** in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_scene.py`. Keep `tab-database-change` unconfigured until initialization finishes. Activate the target workspace and switch its database once. Use a scene-only, one-shot continuation after the real deferred restoration callback and its queued focus application; then request command focus once. Mark initialization complete through a subsequent queued continuation after that focus application. Delegate production restoration unchanged and exactly once.\n- Make readiness observe the intended active workspace, database and command focus. Lost focus must invalidate readiness without refocusing. Preserve existing capture rejection and first-failure evidence. Add no sleeps, arbitrary queue draining, assertion retries or repeated corrective focus requests.\n- **Compare equivalent rendering layers.** Preserve existing `widget_row` and raw-strip observations with their original meaning. Add an explicitly named styled widget row from native `render_lines`, using the widget-local content-region clip and mapping it once to screen coordinates. Compare it strictly with the corresponding compositor crop.\n- Require equal complete text, cell lengths and resolved foreground/background/style flags for styled-widget versus compositor rows. Preserve raw-versus-`render_line` fidelity assertions, exact trailing whitespace, original segments and lengths. Do not manufacture padding, trim whitespace or change ruler output to satisfy equality.\n- Keep diagnostic additions compatible and bounded in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_render_diagnostics.py`. Preserve existing limits, unavailable/incomplete reporting, first-failure snapshots, single-export ownership and atomic publication.\n- **Correct confirmed quality findings:** format `agent_tools/sql_explorer_lifecycle_trace.py` and `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`; resolve their E501 findings without changing output or fixture bytes. Extract cohesive assertion groups from the ruler regression to resolve PLR0915, preserving every assertion and negative control.\n- Update the diagnostic documentation to distinguish raw, styled-widget and compositor layers and explain ordered initialization. Record a concise managed changelog fragment; preserve historical documentation and release entries. Fully read each edited file through its final continuation before writing.\n\nPublic package APIs, production method signatures, dependencies and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without spawning cursors, preserving independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X retain document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve clipboard invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve visible thin primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Retain SQL, colors, widths, selection/scroll/ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture repairs, journal status correction, supersampling, faithful Unicode/style diagnostics, recovered source/docs and current-dev safeguards. Command-caret, secondary-caret and new-file findings remain unresolved until actual candidate evidence supports independent acceptance or a separately reviewed repair.\n\n## Focused regressions and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- Extend the mounted ruler/visual-state regression to prove restoration, queued editor focus, one command-focus request and readiness occur in order. Verify collection preserves focus, text, selections, preferred columns and scroll.\n- Retain independent production tab-focus restoration coverage. Test that later focus loss rejects readiness without another focus request.\n- Test native styled-row/compositor equality across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1, including trailing padding, nonzero origins, gutters, borders and clipping. Preserve raw-strip fidelity, combining marks, wide cells and styles.\n- Retain overlap, shifted mapping, missing-label and missing-gutter controls; extend controls to detect lost trailing cells and incorrect styled-layer colors or flags.\n- First run affected diagnostic, ruler-trace and visual-state modules on canonical Python 3.11 and Python 3.13/3.14 environments, then the supported matrix. Run adjacent multicursor, selection/clipboard, history/reset, caret, completion, journal, menu, checkbox/selector and capture regressions.\n- Require fresh exact-head lint/format/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines. Current failed tests establish no new coverage shortfall.\n- Obtain trusted candidate captures and independently inspect the remaining caret/dialog layers and every one of the **46 full 1280×800 PNGs**, with all geometry checks at **208×47 cells**. Bind evidence to source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Historical captures cannot validate these edits.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent review of this complete plan before coding, followed by complete feature/source and visual review. Assess every diff continuation and companion implementation; distinguish retrieved pages from assessed coverage.\n- Keep existing visual rejections effective until fresh independent review resolves them. Contradictory or inconclusive evidence requires renewed planning, never a forced pass.\n- Preserve complete authenticated history, question/options/answer records, credentials, provenance, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, producer-consumer/exporter compatibility and activation/rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout bytes, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit. Historical pause records neither establish nor release a current hold.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, recommendation-policy companions and every qualifying correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This harness correction alone does not complete that objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a302bef0fb4a29e56cbd7c361d9212f7e8251bf94a8111d0a2c74e4fa738eab0","text":"# Correct PR #9’s quality failures and preserve the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `813432a565124a7f569c38cb6556757ff58cad24` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nComplete current-head records identify two quality failures: import ordering and test formatting. Python matrix, SDK, type, coverage and artifact validation passed. Historical visual findings remain subject to fresh independent review; their older commit associations do not establish current acceptance.\n\nNo material implementation question remains.\n\n## Implementation changes\n\n- In `tests/agent_tools/styled_rows.py`, correct I001 by moving the `SqlExplorerApp` import into the repository first-party import group, after the `agent_tools` imports. Preserve imported symbols and test behavior.\n- Apply canonical Ruff **0.15.22** formatting to `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, following the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character line length and LF configuration. Private workers make source-only edits; verification executes on GitHub.\n- Preserve every test, parameter, assertion, negative control, Unicode fixture, style expectation and diagnostic bound. Add no suppressions, skips or baseline changes.\n- Retain the complete saved checkpoint, recovered source/documentation and chronological task records. Fully read affected files before editing; record the correction through the managed changelog mechanism without changing package or README versions.\n- Preserve public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic schemas and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections across logical lines without adding cursors, preserving independent preferred columns, reversal, clamping and boundaries.\n- Retain independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/undo/redo, bounded history metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empties. Entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor retains whole-buffer copy.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste use matching fragments first, matching lines second while ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve visible primary/secondary underlines over text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Retain SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion suffixes.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture/journal repairs, supersampling, capture safeguards and faithful diagnostics. Retain ordered scene initialization, raw-strip fidelity and strict native-styled-widget/compositor comparisons. This quality correction introduces no additional presentation repair.\n\n## Focused regression and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub.\n\n- First verify import ordering and formatting in the two affected modules, then run the repository quality-debt gate without changing its baselines.\n- Run both existing modules across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1. Retain combining-mark, wide-cell, clipping, trailing-cell, color/style, unavailable-evidence and non-mutation controls, plus production tab-focus restoration coverage. Formatting alone needs no new tests.\n- Run adjacent ruler-trace, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions, followed by focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret and completion coverage.\n- Require fresh final-head lint/format/type, artifact, Python/minimum-dependency matrix, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and existing floors: **98.03% branch, 98.92% combined and 99.22% statement**, plus subsystem floors and debt baselines.\n- Obtain trusted isolated candidate captures at **208×47 cells** and **1280×800 pixels**. Require all **46 geometry checks and individual full-PNG verdicts**, including reassessment of ruler, caret and new-file findings. Preserve picker comparisons and first-failure diagnostics.\n- Bind checks and artifacts to actual source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Inconclusive findings remain unresolved; demonstrated further repairs require renewed independent planning.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent whole-plan review before coding, then complete independent feature/source and visual review. Review every diff continuation and companion implementation; retrieved pages alone do not establish assessed coverage.\n- Preserve current-dev safeguards, authenticated history, credentials, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, dependency barriers—including PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry—and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery and exporter compatibility, activation and rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9, recommendation-policy companions and every qualifying correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete that broader objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"d5a4eb2671dc5a311130ec334a76d39678815f9a1e45b289b3f18673e8418a27","text":"# Correct PR #9’s Ruff failures and retain the complete feature\n\n## Summary\n\nContinue from head `75df835553c7281482c3c66c9ca6a9d94e6fdc83` against pinned dev `f66a80ebe4b3c28dbca17fbc58c2d6ffe464bb01`.\n\nRun `39125605452` identifies three blockers: I001 import ordering, one E501 line, and formatting. Type, coverage, artifacts, Python matrix and SDK checks passed. No material implementation question remains. Historical review findings retain their original commit associations and do not establish current acceptance.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- In `tests/agent_tools/styled_rows.py`, move the `SqlExplorerApp` import immediately after `import pytest`, before the Rich imports. Preserve the separate `agent_tools` group and every imported symbol.\n- In `tests/agent_tools/multicursor_diagnostics.py`, split the line-209 expected findings list across lines, retaining the exact f-string and assertion. Apply canonical Ruff 0.15.22 formatting using the existing Python 3.8 target, 100-character limit and LF configuration.\n- Preserve every test, parameter, Unicode fixture, assertion, negative control and diagnostic bound. Add no suppressions, skips or baseline changes. Formatting alone requires no new tests.\n- Preserve the entire useful checkpoint, recovered source/documentation and authenticated task history. Record a concise managed changelog fragment without changing package or README versions.\n- Public APIs, production behavior, dependencies, diagnostic schemas and Python 3.8–3.14/Textual compatibility remain unchanged. Fully read affected files before editing; reassess changed heads or dev bases.\n\n## Feature contract retained\n\n- Anchored Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down selection without new cursors; independent preferred columns, same-row multicursors, merging, movement, exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles, atomic editing/history, bounded metadata and reset cleanup.\n- Document-order Ctrl+C/`cp`/Ctrl+X fragments, including empties; entirely empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing. One unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Shared keyboard/command/terminal paste precedence: matching fragments, matching lines ignoring one trailing line ending, then whole-text repetition. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Thin primary/secondary underlines over in-document text, spaces and expanded tabs; bars only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, scrolling, ruler mapping and completion.\n- Preserve selected narrow UI/fixture/journal repairs, supersampling, current-dev safeguards, faithful diagnostics, ordered scene initialization, raw-strip fidelity and strict native-styled-widget/compositor comparisons.\n\n## Focused coverage and GitHub validation\n\nAll programs, tests, installs and rendering execute on GitHub; private workers perform source-only work.\n\n- First verify Ruff lint and formatting for both affected modules, then the repository quality-debt gate.\n- Run both existing modules across Textual 0.73.0 and 0.89.1. Retain Unicode/style/clipping/trailing-cell controls, unavailable-evidence reporting, observation non-mutation and production tab-focus restoration coverage.\n- Run adjacent ruler-trace, visual-state and capture-lifecycle regressions, followed by focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret and completion tests.\n- Require fresh final-head quality/type, artifact, compatibility/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Retain canonical coverage JSON and floors of **98.03% branch, 98.92% combined and 99.22% statement**, plus subsystem and debt baselines.\n- Obtain trusted isolated captures at **208×47 cells**, retaining all **46 geometry results and individual full 1280×800 PNG verdicts**, picker comparisons and first-failure evidence. Reassess outstanding ruler, caret and dialog findings independently.\n- Bind evidence to source, checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, run and hashes. Inconclusive findings remain unresolved; further substantive repairs require renewed independent planning.\n\n## Review and completion\n\n- Obtain fresh independent complete-plan review before coding, followed by complete feature/source, companion and visual review. Track assessed diff coverage separately from retrieved pages.\n- Preserve provenance, credentials, genuine-input/security holds, owner veto/cancel, actual operational holds, PR #10’s actual PR #9 ancestry dependency and applicable exact-head protected approvals.\n- The coordinator verifies recommendation-policy/restart/recovery, independent resolver records, exporter compatibility and activation/rollback evidence. Preserve frozen rollout sources, completed deployments, notification limits, concurrency 10, truthful lifecycle labels, authenticated responses and the single 30-minute/open-PR orchestrator with idle exit.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs for PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction PR through successful `dev` merges and required post-merge validation. This formatting correction does not complete that broader objective.\n"},{"approval_index":null,"id":"a0c782b939e10dfbdb8b49208545c316cc542bd48ff9508fe22870b0a712597e","text":"# Complete PR #9’s current-base diagnostic correction\n\n## Summary\n\nPreserve the complete SQL Explorer checkpoint against pinned dev `71422731e51af15a104b65915873d576bf0024c0`.\n\nThe complete assigned feedback and failed-job logs establish import-ordering, formatting and mount-ordering failures at published head `7719e9e18fe98b18ea5ee26c3246dd1341b40f24`. They do not validate the checkpoint’s newer corrections.\n\nThe recorded answers settle the implementation choices. Finish the selected lifecycle correction and diagnostics, obtain fresh GitHub evidence, then independently plan only demonstrated rendering repairs. This plan completes the diagnostic specification; diagnostic success does not complete the parent task.\n\n## Implementation and compatibility\n\n- **Mount ordering:** Preserve and finish the saved work in `agent_tools/sql_explorer_visual_scene.py`. Register the scene’s one-shot action through the intended workspace’s existing `pending_mount_action`. Preserve prior action ownership, single invocation, replacement ownership and exception propagation.\n- Order actual workspace completion and its deferred restoration/focus application before the single database switch. Complete that switch’s restoration before requesting command focus once. Mark initialization complete only after queued command focus applies. Keep production mount/tab/restoration callbacks and ruler presentation unchanged.\n- Readiness must reject later focus loss without repairing it. Retain strict ordering, focus, equality and non-mutation assertions. Add no replacement timer, arbitrary queue drain, repeated refocus, assertion retry or trace filtering.\n- **Quality:** Verify the saved import correction and complete formatting using the repository configuration and pinned Ruff toolchain on GitHub. Preserve every import, fixture byte, parameter, assertion and negative control; introduce no suppression or baseline change.\n- **Caret comparisons:** Finish the SVG-evidence helper and capture integration. For both `keyboard-multicursor` and `editor-command-caret`, retain direct **1280×800**, actual **2560×1600 intermediate**, and once-reduced **1280×800** PNGs under both original and diagnostic-only verified DejaVu Sans Mono declarations: **twelve complete PNGs**.\n- Use identical scene/state inputs for each pair. Change only the identified terminal font declaration in diagnostic variants. Retain exact raw/framed/supersampling SVGs, actual intermediate bytes, dimensions, hashes, lengths, renderer arguments, versions and one Lanczos reduction. Ordinary production output and its invocation remain intact.\n- Retain observed font availability and bounded font-file hashes. Report renderer-selected font identity as unavailable where the API cannot expose it.\n- **Border evidence:** Finish bounded observations for `connections-searching` and `result-success`: actual border geometry, ancestor clips, resolved styles, native styled-widget/compositor edge rows, sampled coordinates and corresponding SVG/full-PNG evidence. Select no production border repair before identifying the failing layer.\n- Preserve raw-strip fidelity alongside strict native-styled-widget/compositor equality, including trailing spaces, combining marks, wide cells and colors/styles.\n- Update focused diagnostic documentation and the existing managed changelog fragment. Preserve recovered source/docs, historical releases, complete task history and current-dev capture/provenance safeguards. Fully read files before editing.\n\nPublic APIs, production signatures, dependencies and Python **3.8–3.14** compatibility remain unchanged. Diagnostic fields are additive; existing fields retain their meanings. Preserve all existing bounds, including separate **4 MiB SVG/decoded-PNG comparison budgets**, reduced-diagnostic limits and exporter **8 MiB per-file / 64 MiB total** limits. Missing, failed or oversized evidence remains incomplete.\n\n## Complete feature contract retained\n\n- Ctrl+Shift+Up/Down extends anchored selections without creating cursors; preserve independent preferred columns, reversal, short-line clamping and boundaries.\n- Preserve independent and same-row multicursors, selection merging, movement/editing and exact-position Shift+Up/Down toggles.\n- Ctrl+C, `cp` and Ctrl+X record document-order fragments, including empties. All-empty multicursor selections clear the clipboard and delete nothing; one unselected cursor copies the whole buffer.\n- Keyboard, command and terminal paste distribute matching fragments first, matching lines second—ignoring one trailing line ending—then repeat the whole text. Preserve metadata invalidation and empty-paste behavior.\n- Preserve atomic undo/redo, shared bounded history recording/pruning and document-reset cleanup.\n- Keep thin primary/secondary underlines over existing text, spaces and expanded tabs, with bars only in padding. Preserve SQL, colors, widths, selections, wrapping, scrolling, ruler/completion mapping and suffixes.\n- Retain selected narrow UI/fixture, journal, new-file, picker, menu, help, find and export repairs, supersampling and ruler reassessment. Partial implementation establishes no additional scope.\n\n## Focused regressions and GitHub acceptance\n\nAll installs, programs, tests, probes and rendering execute through GitHub; private workers perform source-only work.\n\n1. Obtain separate independent review of this complete current-base plan before coding.\n2. Run deterministic delayed-mount coverage first. Prove switching/readiness/capture remain blocked before completion; preserve action ownership and exceptions; require restorations before initialization, exactly one database action and command-focus request, and readiness after actual focus application. Retain later-focus-loss rejection and independent production tab-restoration coverage.\n3. Run caret-stage regressions for exact bytes/hashes, dimensions, declaration-only changes, actual invocation identity, one reduction, non-mutation, missing fonts, renderer failures and exact budget boundaries.\n4. Run border regressions covering coordinates, clipping, Unicode/styles, missing layers, shared bounds and non-mutation. Retain shifted/missing-cell and changed-style negative controls.\n5. Run affected lifecycle, ruler, styled-row, diagnostic and capture suites across Textual **0.73.0** and **0.89.1**, followed by focused selection/multicursor, clipboard, history/reset, caret/completion, journal, menu and checkbox/selector coverage. Keep test modules within repository size limits.\n6. Require exact-final-head lint/format/type, quality, canonical coverage JSON, artifact, supported-Python/minimum-dependency, SDK and aggregate fast checks. Preserve **98.03% branch**, **98.92% combined**, **99.22% statement**, subsystem and debt floors.\n7. Use the existing signed `agent-visual/<candidateSHA>` temporary-candidate route, dispatch to `agent-visual.yml` on main, trusted exporter and geometry-JSON transport. No new dispatcher, native-profile deployment or sidecar transport is required.\n8. Bind evidence to actual source/checkpoint, candidate, base, task, plan, dependencies, producer/consumer revisions, run/job/attempt and artifact hashes. Verify extracted bytes and actual transport sizes.\n9. Independently inspect all twelve full stage PNGs and map the caret cells across stages. Inspect border layers and retain contradictory or inconclusive findings. Underline flags alone cannot establish raster visibility.\n10. After evidence demonstrates a cause, obtain a separate concrete repair plan and independent review before implementing the narrow repair with a meaningful causal regression.\n11. Before correction publication, require complete independent feature/source/companion assessment and all **46 geometry checks plus individual full 1280×800 PNG verdicts at 208×47 cells**. Keep existing rejections effective until fresh acceptance; historical captures cannot certify new content.\n\n## Authority, dependencies and completion\n\n- The inspected prerequisite catalogues establish no upstream peer-merge requirement for PR #9. Do not fabricate `pr_dev_merge` dependencies or treat legacy review migration as satisfaction.\n- Preserve PR #10’s actual PR #9 dev-merge/ancestry requirement and PR #37’s separate dependency on #39. Separate native-profile tasks retain their own scope and approvals.\n- Trusted coordination must recheck current head/base/request, provenance, credentials, authorization and genuine holds at each action boundary. Recorded observations and recommendation selections grant no protected exact-head approval or hold release.\n- Preserve complete questions/options/answers, independent resolver records, owner veto/cancel, frozen rollout bytes and completed/cancelled operations. Do not repeat completed deployments.\n- Retain companion recommendation-policy/restart/recovery and applicable exporter/producer-consumer activation/rollback verification. Preserve authenticated responses, notification limits, concurrency **10**, truthful exclusive lifecycle labels including `agent:writing`, and one **30-minute** orchestrator while qualifying PRs remain open, with idle exit.\n- Continue coordinator monitoring and aligned repairs until PR #9 and every qualifying companion/correction/repair PR merge successfully into `dev` and required post-merge validation completes. This diagnostic checkpoint does not replace that completion requirement.\n"}],"producer_id":"local:e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","questions":[{"answer_index":16,"id":"fbd480038ee660edb95dd3690683161a39480ffc41dfac01f8e147887794ef84","text":"Can the coordinator expose a fresh database-picker capture with its heading widget rows, compositor rows, exported SVG, and hash-bound final PNG through source_files evidence? The available layer evidence is historical, and its PNG is inaccessible. The reviewed plan requires identifying the first failing layer before changing picker presentation or capture/export."},{"answer_index":18,"id":"9a11147e3ffd85ce140c8f1244a1b15377efd00916e606a8b431a2d03a92488d","text":"The fresh receipt binds capture `38731476440` to candidate `3e6d6e980ea7f1e1c3a6412cb9c5cc824aa87df5` and the saved checkpoint. Widget rows, compositor rows and parsed SVG all retain the complete heading, including the `c`. This does not establish a production picker defect.\n\n1. **Coordinator tooling question:** Can `read_evidence_image` be exposed in this planner session for the supplied hash-bound PNG? It is absent from the available tools, and `read_image` returns “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” PNG inspection is still needed before specifying a presentation or export correction.\n\nNo owner decision or replacement upload is needed. Raw SVG bytes are not supplied. The publication transport repair also remains coordinator-owned; complete task history must be preserved."},{"answer_index":19,"id":"16d4d781180edfb004dda9a37d5c640ea072ea2cc5775a4681e92c27f584ab07","text":"Can the coordinator provide the reviewed plan’s GitHub reproduction with actual raw and framed SVG bytes, renderer versions, and available/selected font diagnostics, bound to the candidate, checkpoint and PNG hashes? PNG inspection now works and confirms the obscured `c`; terminal rows and parsed SVG preserve it. The supplied artifacts still cannot distinguish framing from rasterization, so a correction would be speculative."},{"answer_index":20,"id":"9d7dfd33ccfb0fff403dc64cf5154bb0084c6d340b3db71751df45304dbb3650","text":"Coordinator: please expose the exact pre-invocation checkpoint source for tests/agent_tools/render_diagnostics.py. I mistakenly treated a capped 300-line read as complete and omitted its remaining lines when writing. Restore that file’s original suffix before retaining my focused additions. Please also verify the restored README against the saved checkpoint. No owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":21,"id":"962ad2658075e133178b0c27a43c436c00ea5a63640a4a6e0dafbca91a41dc09","text":"Coordinator: please run the approved isolated GitHub candidate capture from the preserved checkpoint, including the restored diagnostic tests and existing SVG-evidence helper/tests. Expose hash-bound database-picker raw/framed SVG content, font/renderer diagnostics and PNG through source_files. The reviewed plan requires this evidence before selecting a heading correction; no owner decision is needed."},{"answer_index":22,"id":"d82141d33b770fcc68e14949f0292959e0f2597aa4301b71d32ab7338f57b0e7","text":"1. The current logs prove checkbox text loss but do not identify its first failing layer; they also report coverage totals without exact missing arcs. Which correction sequence should the plan use?\nEvidence first (Recommended): Fix behavior-preserving Ruff/format issues, add bounded failing-state diagnostics and focused task-related regressions, and obtain exact-head GitHub reproduction plus coverage JSON before selecting a checkbox production repair.\nSeparate diagnostic checkpoint: Keep this step diagnostic-only; obtain checkbox state and coverage evidence on GitHub, then independently plan all lint, test and production corrections together."},{"answer_index":23,"id":"e896f2e46da935a3d8d2023d77a872fd7f6624fbdae4625988d391767b3be2a6","text":"I read the complete current-head check records and all failed-job log parts. Existing feature requirements remain settled; no new owner preference is needed. Three coordinator evidence questions remain before a concrete repair plan:\n\n1. **Picker correction:** Can the coordinator expose capture `38927473247`’s hash-bound receipt, database-picker geometry, complete raw/framed SVGs, and all four comparison PNGs? The visual evidence tools currently return “Source tool unavailable or invalid.” The reviewer’s framing finding needs direct inspection before selecting the export correction.\n\n2. **Coverage:** Can the coordinator expose canonical `coverage.json` from run `38927048857`, bound to head `e3246e88769588cf10b61b5d8de3de1193c43ba2`? Branch coverage is **98.02% against 98.03%**. Exact missing arcs are needed to specify meaningful task-related regressions without changing baselines.\n\n3. **Type-menu failure:** Can the coordinator provide a bounded GitHub reproduction capturing focus, `type_input`, matches, scroll offsets, field/viewport geometry, and queued layout state immediately before the failing initial `assert menu.display` on Python 3.13/3.14? This will distinguish fixture timing from a production positioning defect before choosing a repair.\n\nThese are coordinator artifact requests, not requests for owner uploads or approval. No files were changed and no programs were executed."},{"answer_index":24,"id":"b239df38a3cbbd33de3627b25a36e9063e036dac68b6e9c97c83d69c701c88f3","text":"1. The rejected PNG and widget/compositor rows show `SELECT c.c│FROM`: rendering replaces the existing separator space with a bar. Should the correction preserve every in-document whitespace cell using the thin underline fallback, reserving vertical bars for end-of-line and empty-line padding?\nPreserve whitespace (Recommended): Keep spaces and expanded tabs intact for primary and secondary carets; retain colors, cell widths and completion behavior, and add focused rendering and completion regressions."},{"answer_index":25,"id":"ba800d0ea428ec7a001c0765a90362402cdfe85aa29ac8ae5d7e49a96975ad4b","text":"1. Should the plan restore the newly pinned dev’s capture/export safeguards before completing the outstanding independent review? The current diff deletes `.github/agent/capture_artifact.py`, its regression module and a parent-objective record, reverts `agent-visual.yml`, and removes failed-capture documentation.\nPreserve dev safeguards (Recommended): Restore those files and workflow exactly from pinned dev, retain its documentation plus the feature-specific activation section, preserve the complete SQL Explorer patch, then obtain fresh review and GitHub validation.\nReview before reconciliation: Complete read-only assessment of the published predecessor first; keep current-base reconciliation and final candidate validation blocked until separately planned."},{"answer_index":26,"id":"7955d1db22074defa82b9d57196aac7ba36a0679d4226fe9ad241de670ff3d1e","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve the inherited column ruler and route the reported stray “1” for independent reassessment, using the inspected PNG, separate ruler/editor geometry, identical pinned-dev ruler source, and existing empty-document assertion? This resolves the correction approach only; the rejecting visual gate remains in force until independently reviewed.\nPreserve ruler (Recommended): Preserve production presentation; add a focused tab-switch ruler/gutter regression and explicit scene evidence, then repeat independent full-feature and visual review.\nChange ruler presentation: Authorize a narrow presentation change to distinguish column labels from gutter numbers; its exact appearance needs a further decision before implementation."},{"answer_index":27,"id":"46377a331dc01c2e34cff52b83d9ddd5e5dd1b98a41de0000d6832f0d20a0a45","text":"1. Should the renewed plan first collect bounded, GitHub-only evidence for the indistinct secondary carets before choosing a production or export repair? The inspected PNG confirms the visibility finding, but its geometry does not identify the failing layer.\nDiagnose first (Recommended): Preserve the complete feature and selected ruler work; add exact cursor/focus/scroll state, caret-cell widget/compositor styles and lossless SVG evidence with focused regressions, then independently plan the demonstrated repair after GitHub capture.\nChange caret presentation: Plan a production presentation change now; its precise appearance requires another choice and must preserve SQL, whitespace, colors, widths and mapping."},{"answer_index":28,"id":"1533c21a5bce25f66a9d4d6d9395969fe2d15e25112b4e9000ea13507588cdd7","text":"1. May the renewed plan include narrow repairs for the newly verified journal-error status and new-file dialog alignment, after identifying their failing layers? These extend the earlier enumerated UI repair scope.\nNarrow gate repairs (Recommended): Show read failures without claiming empty results, restore intended dialog centering, add focused regressions, and retain the complete feature and all review gates.\n\n2. Should the correction fix the confirmed diagnostic/test defects and collect missing command-caret and ruler lifecycle evidence before selecting further presentation or focus changes?\nFaithful diagnostics (Recommended): Fix variable shadowing and lint, preserve combining marks and cell styles during cropping, retain strict assertions, and diagnose ruler focus/width and command-caret layers on GitHub without forcing scene state."},{"answer_index":29,"id":"310ef79ccea7f258fef9f5fee47aebad16404f96b3ab0e5fc0e03fac1fad6e90","text":"1. Which correction sequence should the renewed plan specify for the observed ruler focus and row-width failures? Existing assertions and production ruler presentation must remain intact.\nTrace lifecycle (Recommended): Fix the confirmed lint/format findings, preserve current-dev safeguards, and add bounded GitHub-only callback-order and strip-padding observations before selecting the focus or width correction.\nCorrect scene lifecycle: Plan command focus after tab restoration and full-width widget-row collection now; retain strict equality and negative controls, then require GitHub reproduction and independent review."},{"answer_index":30,"id":"fd123ca6bb2e97c0179d0650913397f70c39425e6f71229ff3f98ad248a446a7","text":"1. Should the renewed plan correct the demonstrated harness-layer mismatch: apply the scene’s intended command focus after deferred tab restoration, and compare Textual’s styled widget rows with compositor rows while retaining the original unpadded strips as separate evidence? Production tab behavior and ruler presentation would stay unchanged; strict equality, negative controls, and all feature/review gates remain required.\nCorrect harness layers (Recommended): Use ordered scene initialization and native styled-row collection, preserve raw observations, fix confirmed lint/format findings, and validate on GitHub.\nExtend diagnostics first: Preserve the failing harness and collect native styled-row and focus-application traces on GitHub before separately planning its correction."},{"answer_index":31,"id":"4eabbb1c0750e4fc0765750745d410dec1b52cf5617089e9dfd9c6176b220bff","text":"1. Should the renewed correction replace the tab/database scene’s fixed 0.3-second switch timer with the existing workspace mount-completion hook, ordering database switching after workspace initialization and its deferred restoration, then applying command focus once? The Python 3.12 trace shows workspace completion arriving after scene initialization; preserve every strict ordering assertion, production tab behavior, and the complete feature.\nOrder mount completion (Recommended): Use the existing pending_mount_action hook and ordered scene continuations; add a deterministic delayed-mount regression, correct lint/format findings, and require independent review plus GitHub CI and all 46 visual scenes."},{"answer_index":32,"id":"659c61c7bd86b5bbc53d59c646f62f30d7371c88f1dafedfd973d6d8ac09aa59","text":"1. Should the renewed plan preserve the complete checkpoint and selected mount-ordering correction, fix the confirmed import/format findings, and obtain six GitHub-only caret raster comparisons before selecting an export repair? The latest coordinator report supplies a recommendation, not an approved implementation choice.\nSix comparisons (Recommended): For keyboard-multicursor and editor-command-caret, retain direct, actual 2× intermediate, and reduced PNGs under original declarations and a diagnostic-only verified DejaVu Sans Mono declaration; preserve production rendering, exact SVG/settings/font hashes, bounded lossless evidence, all assertions and review gates."},{"answer_index":33,"id":"706b7cb93eb62f050815bd403f89b787ee00056be012dbafa618eeda9492f614","text":"The feature choices are settled. Current-head run `39133140732` confirms import ordering, formatting, and a mount-ordering failure (`20 < 11`). The saved checkpoint already contains mount-hook work; those earlier failures cannot validate it.\n\nTwo coordinator questions remain before a complete plan can pass independent review. No owner preference or upload is needed.\n\n1. **Capture prerequisites:** Can the coordinator provide current, source-pinned evidence identifying the authorized isolated GitHub capture route, producer/consumer revisions, artifact compatibility, activation state, and applicable operational/protected holds? It must establish whether the selected twelve retained caret-stage PNGs and border diagnostics can be collected without modifying frozen deployments or overriding holds.\n\n2. **Prerequisite representation:** Can the coordinator resolve those external conditions and supply their evidence, or provide a separately reviewed supported mechanism for retaining them in the plan-review contract? The previous independent review rejected the plan because these conditions cannot be represented as `pr_dev_merge`. They must not be omitted or converted into fictitious PR dependencies.\n\nPR #10’s dependency on #9, and #37’s dependency on #39, remain downstream obligations—not prerequisites for #9.\n\nI’m stopping with these evidence questions rather than issuing another plan with unresolved consequential prerequisites. No files were edited or programs executed."}],"replacements":[],"source":"user","starting_prompt":"sql explorer: 1) if ctrl+shift+arrow up/down is pressed, then we should not spawn multiple cursors, instead selection should be expanded to the left until the line start, and next line until cursor's column (vs code like), it can be repeated multiple times to select many lines 2) now it seems that when multiple cursors is spawned, then I ctrl+c something and ctrl+v each cursor inserts WHOLE clipboard. instead each should have its own clipboard (VS code like)","task_id":"e8dd20c11f5043518c59e21e41d4074c","version":2}